The driver allows connecting of multi‐position keylocks over GPIO
pins.   The  keylock  driver  registers with an in‐kernel keylock
supporting system and provides support  through  an  experimental
security  model.   The  keylock  state  can  be queried using the
hw.keylock sysctl variables.  Only locks with 2‐4  positions  are
currently  supported.   The pin number is specified in the kernel
configuration with the locator.  The  locator  denotes  the  pins
used  for the lock (minimum 2, maximum 4 pins are used).  The and
can also be specified when is attached at runtime  using  the  on
